{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q82900150","formula":"C₁₃H₁₅N","hill":"C13H15N","elements":["H","C","N"],"composition":{"C":13.0,"H":15.0,"N":1.0},"names":{"en":"1-(naphthalen-1-yl)propan-2-amine"},"descriptions":{"en":"1-Naphthylaminopropane (1-NAP), also known as 1-naphthylisopropylamine or as α-naphthylaminopropane (α-NAP), is a drug of the amphetamine and naphthylaminopropane families. It is a positional isomer of 2-naphthylaminopropane (2-NAP; PAL-287). 2-NAP and derivatives like methylnaphthylaminopropane (MNAP) are known to be potent serotonin–norepinephrine–dopamine releasing agents (SNDRAs) and/or serotonin receptor agonists, whereas 1-NAP has not been assessed in these regards."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":413939,"mass":185.26,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC(CC1=CC=CC2=CC=CC=C21)N","inchikey":"ODTJDLMNBKMVGR-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"1-naphthalen-1-ylpropan-2-amine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"413939","atoms":29,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":3.888,"y":1.461,"z":-0.098,"el":"N"},{"x":1.858,"y":0.293,"z":-0.855,"el":"C"},{"x":0.616,"y":-0.461,"z":-0.49,"el":"C"},{"x":2.721,"y":0.698,"z":0.357,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.6,"y":0.191,"z":-0.226,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.737,"y":-0.579,"z":0.114,"el":"C"},{"x":0.709,"y":-1.851,"z":-0.42,"el":"C"},{"x":3.218,"y":-0.508,"z":1.154,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.711,"y":1.589,"z":-0.291,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.626,"y":-1.978,"z":0.179,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.41,"y":-2.608,"z":-0.087,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.953,"y":0.072,"z":0.378,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.927,"y":2.219,"z":-0.025,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.046,"y":1.462,"z":0.309,"el":"C"},{"x":2.462,"y":-0.337,"z":-1.526,"el":"H"},{"x":1.625,"y":1.163,"z":-1.48,"el":"H"},{"x":2.139,"y":1.341,"z":1.029,"el":"H"},{"x":1.645,"y":-2.363,"z":-0.629,"el":"H"},{"x":3.917,"y":-0.193,"z":1.939,"el":"H"},{"x":3.739,"y":-1.23,"z":0.516